# Line endings.
#
# The release pipeline runs its shell scripts on Windows too (Git Bash on the
# windows-latest runner), where the checkout defaults to CRLF. Git Bash ignores
# a trailing CR when it PARSES a script, so a CRLF *.sh still runs — but `read`
# does NOT strip it from data, so every blank line in scripts/lib/native_pins.env
# arrived as the variable name CR and killed the Windows release build.
#
# So: everything bash executes or reads is pinned to LF, regardless of the
# checkout's platform defaults.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf
*.env   text eol=lf

# Tree-sitter extraction queries are read at runtime and hashed into the code
# indexer's fingerprint and their bytes are pinned against the compiled-in
# copies (test/tooling/embedded_queries_test.dart). CRLF here would make a
# Windows checkout disagree with every other host.
*.scm   text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts keep CRLF.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
